  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide an effective response and meet the immediate humanitarian needs of Health, Water Sanitation and Health (WASH), Shelter and Protection following Hurricane Matthew in the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity To provide an effective response and meet the immediate humanitarian needs of Health, Water Sanitation and Health (WASH), Shelter and Protection following Hurricane Matthew in the Caribbean is a component of Humanitarian Response to Hurricane Matthew in the Caribbean reported by FCDO with a funding type of 111 - Not for profit organisation and a budget of &#xA3;7,999,998. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Material relief assistance and services.</narrative>
  </description>
